{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GeodesicFaceH3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GeodesicFaceH3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicConformalAngle","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.PiL2"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.norm_hemisphereNormal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.norm_hemisphereNormal","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GeodesicFaceH3.lean#L108-L121","doc":"**The hemisphere normal is a Euclidean unit vector** at a point on the\nhemisphere (radius `R > 0`): `‖p / R‖ = ‖p‖ / R = R / R = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hemisphereNormal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hemisphereNormal","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GeodesicFaceH3.lean#L103-L106","doc":"The Euclidean normal of the hemisphere of radius `R` at a point `p`: the\nradial vector `p / R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hemisphere","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hemisphere","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GeodesicFaceH3.lean#L97-L101","doc":"The **hemisphere** of radius `R`: points of `ℝ³` on the sphere of radius `R`\nabout the origin, at positive height.  (Milnor's normalized position uses\n`R = 1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.norm_verticalPlaneNormal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.norm_verticalPlaneNormal","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GeodesicFaceH3.lean#L81-L89","doc":"**The vertical-plane normal is a Euclidean unit vector** when the base normal\n`n` is a unit vector.  The `z`-component `0` contributes nothing, so the norm is\n`√(n.1² + n.2²) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.mem_verticalPlane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.mem_verticalPlane","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GeodesicFaceH3.lean#L76-L79","doc":"A point is on the vertical plane iff its horizontal projection is on the base\nline — the defining membership, restated for downstream `rw`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneNormal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneNormal","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GeodesicFaceH3.lean#L71-L74","doc":"The Euclidean unit normal of the vertical plane with base normal `n` — the\nhorizontal vector `(n.1, n.2, 0)`, as an element of `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlane","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GeodesicFaceH3.lean#L66-L69","doc":"The **vertical plane** over the base line `{w : w·n = d}` — the set of points\nof `ℝ³` whose horizontal projection lies on that line, at any height. ","signatureChunk":0}]}